Well, you could view any nh game like this, since any 
character could theoretically be killed on level one 
by a newt, given sufficiently bad luck.  Eventually, any 
player will take risks which, strictly speaking, are 
unnecessary (doing Soko, entering the gnomish mines..)  
I think the point is to weigh the risks inherent to each 
alternative, regarding the personal playing style.  Since 
e.g. I can be very slow and careful early on in the game, 
but have the tendency to go a bit rampage when having a 
midlevel char, I think the protection racket might increase 
the overall survival probability of my characters (and I am 
sure about this when it comes to tourists).  One may 
argue that this way I won't learn to be better in midgame, 
but I don't play every game to learn something.  And I 
can ascend atheists, so I don't suck all too bad without 
the racket ;-).

